# Pairs with EventualConvergence. Reproduces current production (#4504): the
# snapshot export skips every key whose value is a tombstone, and the drain
# does not clear the receiver's copy. When the source deletes a key the target
# already holds and then trims its log past the target's cursor, the bootstrap
# carries no row for the key and the stream resumes after the delete, so the
# target keeps the old value forever.
MODULE: EventualConvergenceSnapshotDropsDeletes
TARGET: EventualConvergence
CLASS: Temporal
SUMMARY: the snapshot omits tombstoned rows, so a delete behind the trim point never reaches a re-bootstrapped receiver
PERTURBS: Bootstrap

--- FIND
    /\ val' = [val EXCEPT ![BootTarget] = [k \in Keys |-> @[k] \cup val[BootSource][k]]]
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: a key whose value is a tombstone ships no row.
    /\ val' = [val EXCEPT ![BootTarget] = [k \in Keys |-> @[k] \cup
                  (IF Mode(k) = "lww" /\ ValueAt(BootSource, k, val[BootSource][k]).del THEN {} ELSE val[BootSource][k])]]
--- END
--- FIND
                    @ \cup {<<BootSource, k, Ver(BootSource, k)>> : k \in {j \in Keys : val[BootSource][j] # {}}}]
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: and seeds no identity for it.
                    @ \cup {<<BootSource, k, Ver(BootSource, k)>> : k \in {j \in Keys : val[BootSource][j] # {}
                                                                        /\ ~(Mode(j) = "lww" /\ ValueAt(BootSource, j, val[BootSource][j]).del)}}]
--- END
